## Notes

- D_A2 (parameter-count normalised) multiplies S_V/S_L by n_L/n_V = 63,428,096/87,849,216 = 0.722. Pairs with 1 < S_V/S_L < 1.385 therefore change sign: here Flowers102->EuroSAT (ratio 1.193; correct under D_A, wrong under D_A2) and Flowers102->DTD (ratio 1.190; wrong under D_A, correct under D_A2). The total stays 7/12 by coincidence. D_A2 is a monotone function of D_A, so AUROC and Spearman are identical; the sign accuracy is not guaranteed to be.

## Verdict

**DEV FAIL: negative result** (primary D_A: 7/12, AUROC 0.778).

## Caveats

> Exploratory: 12 pairs from 4 datasets (not independent), single seed. These 12 pairs are a development set already used by the gap and gradient-interference signals. A dev pass is 'promising on dev only', not a confirmation.

